# Repository root = the AcouDiet project itself (ADR-51).
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS THE MOST IMPORTANT ONE IN THE REPO (ADR-36, re-pointed by ADR-51)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project had **no version control at all** until ADR-36, and its own ADR log records at least
# two irreversible losses caused by that -- e.g. "旧包已被 Copy-Item 覆盖，本仓不是 git 仓库，
# 取不回旧字节", and ADR-34's Qwen removal had to be hand-archived before anything could be deleted.
#
# The reason nobody had committed is visible below: the tree carries tens of GB of build output and
# vendored toolchains. Ignoring the heavy directories makes the real sources (a few MB) committable.
#
# ADR-51 moved the code from `AcouDiet/` up to the repository root and renamed the old
# `AcouDiet/docs/` to `records/`, so that a clone is a normal single-project checkout. Every rule
# below was re-pointed in that same commit; the build/gate scripts derive their own root from their
# file location, so only this file and a handful of literal paths had to change.

# ---- Toolchains (outside the deliverable on purpose) -------------------------------------
# `_toolchain/` is this machine's self-contained dev environment (~26 GB: Flutter, JDK 17, a
# portable CPython + site-packages, the Android SDK). It is an environment fact, not source.
# Every entry point honours ACOUDIET_TOOLCHAIN / ACOUDIET_PYTHON / ACOUDIET_FLUTTER so another
# machine can point at its own checkout -- see README section "环境".
_toolchain/
# Leftover Android SDK copy that predates the consolidation into `_toolchain/`.
AcouDiet/_toolchain/
*.gguf

# ---- Build output ------------------------------------------------------------------------
app/build/
app/.dart_tool/
app/.flutter-plugins
app/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
app/.packages
build/
_build/
ai/data/raw/
ai/data/augmented/
ai/data/parity_out/

# ---- Review artefacts --------------------------------------------------------------------
# `app/tool/visual_capture_test.dart` renders the real pages to PNG so the UI work can be reviewed
# against `design/软件UI界面设计图/*.png` without a device (ADR-38). The renders are derived output:
# one command regenerates them, and the *checks* that must stay green are the widget tests, not the
# pixels.
app/tool/visual_capture/
# Same job, different directory: on a mismatch the same test writes master/test/masked/isolated
# PNGs into `tool/failures/`. Measured 2026-09-15: 25 files, ~6 MB, pure derived output -- and the
# old rule above did not cover it, so it was staged for the first push.
app/tool/failures/

# ---- Derived measurement intermediates ---------------------------------------------------
# The per-sample probability dump behind `ai/reports/threshold_calibration.md` (FF-20b). It is a
# 173 KB intermediate of a specific model sha256 and is regenerated in one command:
#   python tool/evaluate_shipped_model.py --predictions ai/artifacts/shipped_predictions.jsonl
# The *report* it feeds is committed, because FF-20b requires the calibration process to be
# written down; the dump is not, because it would silently go stale against a new model.
ai/artifacts/shipped_predictions.jsonl
ai/artifacts/*.keras
ai/artifacts/saved_model/

# ---- Release artifacts -------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⚠️ MEASURED BEFORE THE FIRST PUSH (ADR-50): the rules below used to name `dist/` only, while
# `build_release.ps1` had been changed (ADR-44, section "archive index") to write into
# `docs/release/` -- and the tree was later consolidated into `release/`. So the ignore rule stopped
# matching the directory that actually held the output, and 1.95 GB of APKs became committable,
# including TWO 568 MB files. GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB, so the first `git push` would
# have failed outright -- after uploading everything before it.
#
# The rule is now written against the EXTENSION, not one directory, so a future move of the archive
# cannot silently reopen the hole. What stays COMMITTED is the ledger: `release/RELEASE_*.md`,
# `release/apk_sha256.txt` and `release/analyze_*.txt`. Those record which bytes were ever released;
# the APKs themselves are rebuildable from source + the model card.
#
# See ADR-36 for the honest limitation of this choice: a *rebuilt* APK still overwrites its
# predecessor, so the hash ledger is what preserves "which bytes were ever released".
*.apk
*.aab
release/dist/*.apk.sha256

# ---- Android / Gradle / signing ----------------------------------------------------------
app/android/.gradle/
app/android/local.properties
app/android/key.properties
app/android/app/debug/
app/android/app/profile/
app/android/app/release/
*.jks
*.keystore

# ---- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# ---- Large binaries that are inputs, not source ------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.docx
# Training/inference checkpoints: 511 MB and 31 MB here, and the on-device language model they
# belonged to was removed in ADR-34. `*.tflite` files are deliberately NOT ignored -- they are
# the shipped artifact (4 MB) and committing them is what makes a rebuild reproducible.
*.safetensors
tokenizer.json

# ---- Deliberately NOT published (ADR-51) -------------------------------------------------
# Local planning/working material the project owner chose to keep off the public repository. It
# stays on disk; these rules mean it can never be committed by accident.
/讨论资料/
/建议模型/

# ---- Editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
